gh diplomatic uh gold to be had from  taking such an operation  and it's working hard to avoid any  military confrontations from its  presence there  is turkey seeking to expand its  influence in afghanistan and  would what would it stand to gain  well undoubtedly turkey has been working  very hard all across central asia  playing the ethnic turkic card in those  countries to build its influence to  build economic and diplomatic ties and  having  a key role in afghanistan will certainly  enhance those efforts  turkey has built very close ties with  afghans afghanistan's neighbor  uzbekistan and it's looking beyond those  countries as well  but i think the key goal for this whole  operation is to repair ties with the  united states  the u.s has a number of issues with  turkey it was poised to give sanctions  against turkey would devastate the  turkish economy  playing this key role which effectively  gives the u.s a get out of jail card  free  from a major diplomatic crisis will see  turkey  reminding washington it's a key ally and  it needs to work with turkey  dorian thanks ali i'll turn to you the  taliban is advancing almost  unopposed what's the feeling there in  government held  areas  um i wouldn't say they're advancing  unopposed you know there is a government  effort to fight back against them there  are people upper  people's uprising movements fighting  back against them and as much as we hear  reports of districts falling to them we  also hear reports of those districts  being regained everything is sort of an  overdrive at the moment um but there is  you know  this fear that if they are able to so  quickly  trade uh hands with districts you know  from  the government to the taliban and back  and forth uh  that what's to keep them from coming to  kabul at this point there's no real  evidence that they could actually  breach all of the security barriers and  actually make it into the city of kabul  but that fear definitely does exist at  the moment for people  will therefore the turkish troops  increase security in the long term  especially given that the taliban has  said that any foreign troops including  turkish ones will be seen as invaders  well the thing is that the turks have  always had  a unique relationship in afghanistan  they've been very close with the  government  they haven't necessarily been  adversarial with the taliban and the way  other  uh troops have been i mean if you look  at the history of the turkish presence  in afghanistan  they've only come under attack once  maybe twice  and the entire time that they've been  here and turkey is trying to be very  pragmatic and smart about the role it's  playing in afghanistan  it seems to want to keep every party in  the country happy  and if you look at the statements that's  come out with recently since the  announcement of the us withdrawal  they keep saying that they can be like  the one true partner for afghanistan  the one country that can work with them  that can provide services  that can really ally with them right ali  latifi in kabul and dorian jones in  istanbul thank you to you both  you
 

